<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<worksheet>
  <title>Second Fundamental Theorem of Calculus (Section 5.2)</title>

  <exercise>
    <task workspace="1in">
      <statement>
        <p>Shown below on the left is the graph of a function <m>g(t)</m>.</p>
        <p><image source="figures/03-ftc-graph.eps"/></p>
        <p><image source="figures/03-ftc-graph-empty.eps"/></p>
        <p>We will define a new function by
  <md>
  A(x) = \int_1^x g(t)~dt.
  </md></p>
        <p>Let's begin by evaluating <m>A(2) = \int_1^2g(t)~dt</m>.</p>
      </statement>
    </task>
    <task workspace="1in">
      <statement>
        <p>Find the exact values of <m>A(x)</m> to complete the table below.</p>
        <p>\begin{tabular}{|c||c|c|c|c|c|c|c|c|}
      \hline
      <m>x</m> \vphantom{\Huge M}&amp; 0 &amp; 1 &amp; 2 &amp; 3 &amp; 4 &amp; 5 &amp; 6 &amp; 7 
      \hline
      <m>A(x)</m> \vphantom{\Huge M}
                            &amp; 
                                &amp; 
                                    &amp; 
                                        &amp; 
                                            &amp; 
                                                &amp; 
                                                    &amp; 
                                                        &amp;  
      \hline
    \end{tabular}</p>
        <p>Sketch a graph of <m>A(x)</m> on the right above.</p>
        <p>On what intervals is <m>A</m> increasing and how does this relate to the
  behavior of <m>g</m>?  Also, on what intervals is 
  <m>A</m> decreasing?</p>
      </statement>
    </task>
    <task workspace="1in">
      <statement>
        <p>Where does <m>A</m> have a relative minimum or maximum?  How is this
  related to the value of <m>g</m>?</p>
      </statement>
    </task>
    <task workspace="1in">
      <statement>
        <p>Remembering that <m>A</m> is an antiderivative of <m>g</m>, what is the value
  of the derivative <m>A'(1)</m>?</p>
      </statement>
    </task>
    <task workspace="1in">
      <statement>
        <p>%</p>
      </statement>
    </task>
  </exercise>

  <exercise>
    <task workspace="0.75in">
      <statement>
        <p>Suppose that <m>g</m> is the function whose graph is shown on the
%   left below and that we define
%   <md>
%   A(x)= \int_1^x g(t)~dt.
%   </md></p>
        <p>%   
%     <image source="figures/04-ftc-example-1.eps"/>
%     
%     <image source="figures/04-ftc-example-2.eps"/>
%</p>
        <p>%   What is the value <m>A(2)</m>?  Explain your thinking.</p>
        <p>%</p>
      </statement>
    </task>
    <task workspace="0.75in">
      <statement>
        <p>%   What is the value <m>A'(2)</m>?  Explain your thinking.</p>
        <p>%</p>
      </statement>
    </task>
    <task workspace="0.75in">
      <statement>
        <p>%   Is <m>A</m> increasing or decreasing at <m>x=2</m>?  Explain your thinking.</p>
        <p>%</p>
      </statement>
    </task>
    <task workspace="0.75in">
      <statement>
        <p>%   On what interval(s) is <m>A</m> increasing?  decreasing?</p>
        <p>%</p>
      </statement>
    </task>
    <task workspace="0.75in">
      <statement>
        <p>%   
%   On what interval(s) is <m>A</m> concave down?  concave up?</p>
        <p>%</p>
      </statement>
    </task>
    <task workspace="0.75in">
      <statement>
        <p>%   Where does <m>A</m> have a relative minimum?  relative maximum?</p>
        <p>%</p>
      </statement>
    </task>
    <task workspace="1in">
      <statement>
        <p>%   What is the maximum value of <m>A</m> on the interval <m>[-1,4]</m> and where
%   does it occur?  What is
%   the minimum value and where does it occur?</p>
        <p>%</p>
      </statement>
    </task>
    <task workspace="1in">
      <statement>
        <p>%   Sketch an accurate graph of <m>A</m> on the right above.</p>
      </statement>
    </task>
  </exercise>

  <exercise>
    <task workspace="1in">
      <statement>
        <p>The <em>Fresnel integral function</em> is defined by
  <md>
  S(x) = \int_0^x \sin(t^2)~dt
  </md>
  and is used in the study of optics.</p>
        <p>What is <m>S(0)</m>?</p>
      </statement>
    </task>
    <task workspace="1in">
      <statement>
        <p>Use some computational device (maybe your calculator or Desmos) to 
  estimate <m>S(1)</m>.</p>
      </statement>
    </task>
    <task workspace="1in">
      <statement>
        <p>What is <m>S'(1)</m>?  Is <m>S(x)</m> increasing or decreasing at <m>x=1</m>?</p>
      </statement>
    </task>
    <task workspace="1in">
      <statement>
        <p>Find the first relative maximum to the right of <m>x=0</m>.  What is the
  value of <m>S</m> at this relative maximum?</p>
      </statement>
    </task>
    <task workspace="1in">
      <statement>
        <p>Find the first relative minimum to the right of <m>x=0</m>.  What is the
  value of <m>S</m> at this relative maximum?</p>
      </statement>
    </task>
    <task workspace="1in">
      <statement>
        <p>Find the second relative maximum to the right of <m>x=0</m> and the value
  of <m>S</m> at this relative maximum.</p>
      </statement>
    </task>
    <task workspace="2in">
      <statement>
        <p>Sketch the graph of <m>S(x)</m> below.</p>
      </statement>
    </task>
  </exercise>

  <exercise>
    <task workspace="1in">
      <statement>
        <p>The function
  <md>
  E(x) = \int_0^x e^{-t^2}~dt
  </md>
  appears frequently in probability and statistics and is closely
  related to an important function called the <em>error function</em>.</p>
        <p>What is the derivative <m>E'(1)</m>?</p>
      </statement>
    </task>
    <task workspace="1in">
      <statement>
        <p>Use some computational device to
  estimate the value <m>E(1)</m>.</p>
      </statement>
    </task>
    <task workspace="1in">
      <statement>
        <p>Explain why <m>E</m> is an always increasing function.</p>
      </statement>
    </task>
    <task workspace="1.5in">
      <statement>
        <p>Sketch the graph of <m>E(x)</m> below.</p>
      </statement>
    </task>
  </exercise>

</worksheet>
